      "year": 2013,
      "abstract": "Detecting anomalies and the subsequent determination of their causes during satellite mission operations is often a time-consuming and manpower-wise demanding task. ADIA (Autonomous Diagnostic System for Nanosatellites) is a project jointly undertaken by the Chair of Aerospace Information Technology and the Chair of Information Systems at the University of Wuerzburg aiming to design an onboard software system capable of autonomously analyzing a satellite's housekeepings, detecting anomalies based on this data and isolating their cause in a fully autonomous way in real time. ©2013 by the International Astronautical Federation. All rights reserved.",
